{"@context":["https://litlfred.github.io/folio-assistant/ns/content/v1.jsonld",{"@base":"https://litlfred.github.io/folio/"}],"@id":"papers/quantum-observable-universe/blocks/ex-q-reeb-vector-field","@type":["folio-assistant-core:Example","doco:Section"],"label":"ex:q-reeb-vector-field","kind":"example","title":"$q$-Deformed Reeb vector field","uses":["papers/quantum-observable-universe/blocks/ex-q-lie-bracket"],"interprets":"papers/quantum-observable-universe/blocks/def-categorical-reeb","tags":["reeb","archimedean"],"leanRef":"qou:QOU.qReebVectorField","text":"q-reeb-vector-field.md","leanSource":"folio/quantum-observable-universe/quantum-observable-universes/q-reeb-vector-field.lean","provenance":"authored","html":"<a id=\"ex:q-reeb-vector-field\"></a><p>The categorical Reeb derivation <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">\\xi</code> deforms in the archimedean setting to <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">\\xi_q</code>, acting on smooth functions <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">f \\in C^\\infty(M)</code> by</p>\n<pre><code class=\"language-math math-display\">  \\xi_q(f) =  q^{-1}\\xi(f) + (1 - q^{-1})[\\xi, X_f]_q,</code></pre>\n<p>where <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">X_f</code> is the horizontal lift of <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">\\mathrm{grad}_{g_\\varTheta}f</code> to <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">\\ker\\varTheta</code>.</p>\n","source":"folio/quantum-observable-universe/quantum-observable-universes/q-reeb-vector-field.md","heading":"Example","number":"3.19.4"}
